  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Paper & Signal",
    "overview": "Creative North Star: **Paper & Signal**. Updated 2026-11-03. One identity for\npublic discovery, account flows and the creator dashboard: a cool paper ground,\nwhite panels, navy ink and a single blue signal, softened with rounded controls,\nlight panel shadows and pastel tints.\n\nThe direction is inspired by the calm, card-led feel of anicards.ir. It is\ninspired by, not copied: no logo, wordmark, copy, imagery, illustration or\ncomponent is taken from that site. Only generic qualities — cool grey palette,\nnavy/blue pairing, 8/12/16 radii, pill chips, soft shadows, pastel cards — carry\nacross.\n\nThis retires the previous \"Datasheet\" rules. Square controls, ruled-only\nstructure, the ban on shadows and the zero-radius dashboard override are no\nlonger the house style. What survives from the Datasheet is its discipline:\nGeist and Estedad, dense but legible type, explicit trust metadata, visible\nstate labels and restrained motion. Do not revive the older \"Signal & Void\"\nserif, gradients, glass panels, glow or scroll entrances either.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool paper ground, navy ink and blue signal.",
      "Rounded controls and restrained panel shadows.",
      "Explicit trust/provenance and readable EN/FA workflows.",
      "Separate warm editorial blog with shared accessibility and interaction requirements."
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the existing tokens and components, consistent peer-section spacing,   explicit trust labels, readable fields and both marketplace themes.",
      "Do preserve the blog's confirmed editorial palette/type while sharing   accessibility, interaction, responsive and RTL requirements.",
      "Do record observed defects separately from the intended rule and verify   the actual rendered result after a repair."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't restore square Datasheet panels, Signal & Void effects or another   competing visual system from stale comments, previews or tests.",
      "Don't make every button blue, turn every status green, or use arbitrary   color choices as unchecked text/action foregrounds.",
      "Don't hide failed requests behind empty messages or synthetic content,   weaken authorization, discard form state, or count a clean detector as proof   that every screen is accessible."
    ]
  }
}
